<HTML>
<P>You may "drag-n-drop" the program icon to your desktop or dock.

<P>You may also drag-n-drop the "Wang600Files" folder to your home directory,
or other location, to get the sample programs. This folder is also used
to store any programs you create. If another location is chosen,
the environment variable WANG600HOME must be set to that path.
This can be done by using the Property List editor as follows:
<OL>
<LI>Right click on the program icon, on your desktop or dock, and select Show Package Contents.
<LI>Enter the "Contents" folder.
<LI>Open the "Info.plist" file.
<LI>Look for the "LSEnvironment" item, expand it, and edit the
item for "WANG600HOME".
</OL>

<P>The Uninstall item in this package may be used to uninstall this program,
or you can simply move the program icon, from desktop or dock, to the trash.
</HTML>
